A story from my own adventures in those gnomish mines: You know that maybe
you should quit the mines when you enter a big cavern where a red AND a green
dragon are sitting next to each other peacefully sharing their treasure pile...
but then again, didn't that other gnome over there just deliberately step
onto a polymorph trap (turning into a newt, hehe)? Now that we at least
*know* how this happened, couldn't we do something about it short of stepping
into it?

Well how about *using* it against the baddies .. or at least try if it works.
Hmm since the red one of the dragons twinkles at me rather peacefully I decide
to give it a chance and step right behind that polymorph trap (not without
the green dragon biting me a few times along the way), but 'lo! WOPP it says
as the dragon blindly clips that last turn I made ... must have forgotten
about the trap ... well I hear being polymorphed affects your memory ...
and turns into a MUMAK!

Huh oh well I'll be able to stand half a dozen more mumak attacks and since
upon that shock I already had taken back a step allowing the mumak to follow
and *BUTT!* kick at me I'll try the same again (the odds are for something
MANAGEABLE this time right?), pass the mumak *OUCH* *OUCH* *OUCH* and hope-
fully step behind that foul trap ... WOPP!

I barely dare to glance through my fingers, but that's hardly necessary: Us
experienced adventurers can smell a Minotaur's stink hundred yards against
the wind, right? All what's left to say is that I think nethack enjoys this,
or what would *you* say if it told you you were lucky after THAT?

